+# rpc-gossip-bridge — RESULT (2026-10-23 ~02:20Z)
+
+**Status: source plus offline tests only. Nothing deployed, no live P2P probe in this step, no production action, no SSH,
+no transactions, no keys, no chain sync.** I did not edit, build in or message worker A's trees (`rpc-priority/repo`,
+`rpc-priority/helios-patched`).
+
+## What it is
+
+`network/gossip-head-source.mjs` is the narrow adapter between the tested native listener and A's existing Helios head
+relay. It runs `enclave-base-head-listener` (head-listener `f3159ea`, binary sha256 `8ef3d51d…`) as an owned child
+process. It turns each head the listener accepted into the Helios `SequencerCommitment`
+(`{data: parentBeaconRoot ‖ SSZ payload, signature: {r, s, yParity}}`) that `op-head-relay.mjs` already verifies and
+serves to Helios through `--consensus-rpc http://127.0.0.1:<port>/`. **No hosted consensus URL** is involved: the relay
+is created with `sources: []`, and the native source feeds it through `relay.offer`.
+
+Tier: `unsafe`, finality: `none`. A head means only that the administrator-pinned sequencer key signed that block.
+
+## Checks per head (all must pass; otherwise the head is dropped and counted)
+
+1. **Session start record:** `schema enclave-base-unsafe-head/v1`, pinned `chainId`, pinned `signer` with
+   `signerSource=admin-pin`, `baseSourceCommit 5476069f…` and the listener's object encoding. A mismatch ends the
+   session before any head is used.
+2. **Head record:**
+   * unsafe/none labels, pinned chain and signer, `payloadVersion v4`, well-formed hashes;
+   * `objectBytes` ≤ 10 MiB;
+   * `receivedUnixMs` ≥ the session start, so a replay from an earlier run is refused.
+3. **Object file:** the session's own `<sha256>.v4.snappy`. Its size and sha256 must equal the record.
+4. **Native verification:** the **real pinned listener's `verify-object`** (maintained base/base signer, chain domain
+   and block-hash check) must accept the file and report the same number, hash, stateRoot and signer. Bounds: 10 s
+   timeout, 64 KiB output.
+5. **Decode:** a bounded raw-snappy decode (`network/snappy-raw.mjs`, capped at base's 10 MiB). Then `data` = bytes
+   65 onward, and the signature is the first 65 bytes.
+6. **Reviewed verifier:** A's `verifyCommitment` (viem `recoverAddress`) must recover the pinned signer for the pinned
+   chain. The decoded number, hash, stateRoot, parentHash and timestamp must equal the record.
+7. **Freshness:** the signed block timestamp must be within `maxHeadAgeMs` (default 60 s) of now and at most 5 s in the
+   future. It is checked before and after the native round trip. The relay then applies its own freshness check,
+   equivocation check and refusal of transaction types the verifier can't decode.
+
+Validation is never downgraded. There is no fallback source of any kind, and freshness always comes from the signed
+timestamp. A restart cannot make an old head fresh: each session gets a new empty object directory, and records stamped
+before the session started are refused.
+
+## Lifecycle and bounds
+
+* **Owned child:**
+  * spawned `detached`, so it has its own process group;
+  * identity recorded as pid, pgid and `/proc` start time;
+  * environment limited to PATH, an isolated per-session HOME and RUST_LOG=warn;
+  * the binary's sha256 is checked before **every** spawn, and a mismatch means no start.
+* **Signalling:** only the leader whose start time still matches, or surviving members of its group created after it.
+  A recycled PID is never signalled; zombies count as gone.
+* **Stop:** SIGTERM, then SIGKILL after 5 s, then a sweep of the owned group. `stop()` resolves after the last
+  delivery, and the session directory is removed.
+* **Restarts:** backoff of 1, 2, 5, 15 and 60 s, reset after a delivery. A listener with no delivered head for
+  `restartIfNoHeadMs` (default 120 s) is restarted. `status().fresh` turns false `staleAfterMs` (default 30 s) after
+  the last delivery, or as soon as the head is older than `maxHeadAgeMs`.
+* **Buffers:**
+  * stdout line ≤ 16 KiB (a longer line ends the session);
+  * stderr keeps only a 16 KiB tail;
+  * at most 32 queued heads (extra ones are dropped and counted);
+  * at most 16 queued archive entries.
+* **Disk:** each object is deleted as soon as it has been processed, so disk use is bounded by in-flight objects.
+* **Archiving:** an optional `onArchive` hook, for example Sia, is downstream and fire-and-forget. It gets the bytes in
+  memory and never delays serving (tested with a hook that never resolves). Neither Sia nor RPC is needed to bootstrap.
+
+## Test evidence (shared queue, terminal results)
+
+All runs: `jobs/run-q.sh` → `claude-test-queue.py --mib 768` with the 16 GiB floor, inside `unshare -r -n` with `lo`
+up. The script and test 1 both assert that no external route or network exists. The real listener binary's sha256 is
+checked first.
+
+| Run | Result | Peak RSS | What changed |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| r1 | 14/18 pass, rc 1 | 200 MiB | My bugs: `verify-object` ran with an env that dropped the test double's delegate variable (fail-closed: every head refused); a wrong test vector; a per-file test timeout |
+| r2 | 26/28, rc 1 | 276 MiB | A test bug: the pin-mismatch record also mismatched the signer field, so it never reached the native check |
+| r3 | 27/28, rc 1 | 278 MiB | **Finding:** flipping the middle byte of object 52965076 is a different snappy encoding of the *identical* signed envelope. It was correctly accepted as that genuine block, so the test was wrong. Split into two tests |
+| r4 | 29/29, rc 0 | 349 MiB | — |
+| r5 | 29/29, rc 0 | 329 MiB | The re-encoding test made strict (deterministic for the fixture) |
+| **r6** | **29/29, rc 0, 13.1 s** | **285 MiB** | Objects deleted after processing (final code) |
+
+The 29 tests cover:
+* **Real Base mainnet data:** 3 captured objects (blocks 52965074, 52965075 and 52965076, from the 2026-10-23T01:37Z
+  live run). They are verified by the real `verify-object`, decoded, and recover Base's signer
+  `0xaf6e…9e8a` through A's verifier. The relay serves 52965076.
+* **Rejections:**
+  * stale and later-stale heads;
+  * 5 start-record mismatches: signer, chain, not an admin pin, other source commit, other schema;
+  * 8 record mismatches: signer, chain, tier ×2, version, previous-session stamp, oversized object, stateRoot
+    disagreeing with native verification;
+  * object attacks: signature-byte flip (refused by the real verifier), truncation (refused by the real verifier),
+    missing file, size mismatch, digest mismatch;
+  * a genuine object under a different pinned signer (refused by the real verifier).
+* **Restart replay:** later sessions replaying the same genuine block cannot make it fresh.
+* **Lifecycle:**
+  * SIGKILL death followed by a restart;
+  * group kill of leader and grandchild;
+  * refusing to signal an identity that doesn't match;
+  * a line flood;
+  * a silent listener (restart);
+  * a digest mismatch (never started);
+  * a stuck archive hook;
+  * the **real listener's offline lifecycle**: start record accepted, 0 heads, exit 3 recorded, restart scheduled.
+* **Snappy:** all 3 real objects; truncation at about 1,000 cut points; length cap; bad offsets; overrun; early end; an
+  overlapping copy; and a 200-case seeded corruption fuzz. Every case either throws, decodes to identical bytes, or
+  fails signature recovery.
+
+**Not tested here:**
+* Live peers: no further probe was authorized, and the listener's own live evidence is in
+  `../rpc-peer-audit/RESULT.md` §10.
+* Running Helios against this adapter: A's tree owns that end-to-end test.
+* Denim 200 ms rates.
+
+## Integration instructions (for root and A after A's current work is terminal)
+
+1. **Copy into `rpc-priority/repo`** (new files; nothing existing is modified):
+   * `network/gossip-head-source.mjs`
+   * `network/snappy-raw.mjs`
+   * `test/gossip-head-source.test.mjs`
+   * `test/snappy-raw.test.mjs`
+   * `test/fixtures/fake-listener.mjs` (keep it executable)
+   * `test/fixtures/listener-start-record.json`
+   * `test/fixtures/base-mainnet-5296507{4,5,6}.{head.json,v4.snappy.hex}`
+
+   **Do not** copy `network/op-head-relay.mjs` or `network/rpc-identity.mjs`. They are byte-identical copies of A's
+   `97785a40c` versions (sha256 `ed71c069…` and `74cb965e…`, unchanged at A's `36a83c89b`). If A changes
+   `op-head-relay.mjs`, re-run the tests: the adapter uses only `verifyCommitment`, `relay.offer` and `payloadHead`.
+2. **No new npm dependency.** The adapter uses only Node built-ins plus viem through `op-head-relay.mjs` (viem 2.53.1,
+   locked in A's `package-lock.json`).
+3. **Native binary:** build head-listener at `f3159ea` (`tools/prepare-upstream.py` plus `build.sh`; see its
+   `INTEGRATION.md`) and require sha256 `8ef3d51d8767a66fddef7727837737890c2c6e4ff860df1add6aadb0f5581974`
+   (`TESTED_LISTENER_SHA256`). Tests expect it at `artifacts/enclave-base-head-listener`. Adjust `REAL` in
+   `test/gossip-head-source.test.mjs` to the in-repo artifact path.
+4. **Run the tests the way A's `jobs/witness-tests-r2.sh` does:** `unshare -r -n`, `ip link set lo up`, then
+   `node --test --test-force-exit --test-concurrency=1 --test-timeout=300000 test/snappy-raw.test.mjs test/gossip-head-source.test.mjs`.
+   Queue at 768 MiB; the peak was 285–349 MiB.
+5. **Wiring** (administrator pin; no hosted URL):
+   ```js
+   const relay = createHeadRelay({ sources: [], chainId: 8453, signer: adminPinnedSigner, maxAgeMs: 60000 });
+   const consensusRpc = await relay.listen(0);            // 127.0.0.1 only -> Helios --consensus-rpc
+   const gossip = createGossipHeadSource({ listenerPath, listenerSha256: TESTED_LISTENER_SHA256, chainId: 8453,
+     signer: adminPinnedSigner, workDir, onCommitment: (c) => relay.offer(c, 'native-gossip'), onArchive /* optional */ });
+   await gossip.start();   // gossip.status() for health; gossip.stop() on shutdown or abort
+   ```
+   * `adminPinnedSigner` comes from administrator configuration, never from peers or chain advertisements. Today it
+     is `0xaf6e19be0f9ce7f8afd49a1824851023a8249e8a` (base/base `config.rs:500`, matches A's `BASE_MAINNET`).
+   * Rotation means a config change and a restart. L1 SystemConfig rotation tracking is not implemented.
+   * Keep `workDir` on the storage that hosting policy allows (not an NVMe hosting allocation). Contents are transient
+     and bounded.
+
+## Limits and uncertainty
+
+* **Availability:** availability equals the listener's live behaviour. In the one 120 s live run, the v4 mesh never
+  exceeded 1 peer and all 5 published bootnodes failed from this site. Longer-term availability is UNMEASURED.
+* **Restarts lose head continuity:** each session lasts at most `sessionSecs` (≤ 3600). A new ephemeral identity must
+  rediscover peers, which took about 10–20 s in the live run. During that time the relay may serve nothing (fail
+  closed). Gap behaviour over many restarts is unmeasured.
+* **Denim (2026-11-05, 200 ms blocks):**
+  * the per-head `verify-object` spawn and the queue cap of 32 are untested at 5 heads/s;
+  * when the queue is full, new heads are dropped rather than old ones;
+  * the listener's `--max-output-bytes` must be raised (it counts all bytes written; at about 325 KB/s the 64 MiB
+    default lasts about 200 s before the listener exits and restarts).
+* **Object identity for archiving:** the compressed object's sha256 is **not** a unique block identifier, because
+  different snappy encodings of the same signed block exist (observed in r3). Sia or any downstream archive should
+  key by block hash (or sha256 of the decoded envelope) and re-verify on read.
+* **Unsafe tier only:** no finality, possible unsafe reorgs, no state. Fresh state witnesses still need a JSON-RPC
+  proof source.
+* **Self-written codec:** the snappy decoder is written here, not taken from a maintained library (none is installed,
+  and adding one was avoided). It is defended in depth: native verification first, signature recovery over the exact
+  decoded bytes after, plus truncation and fuzz tests. A decoder fault can only refuse a head; it cannot accept a
+  wrong one.
